{"commit": "aeef0be672538b8f6694f464bd947084813fb327", "id": "aeef0be672538b8f6694f464bd947084813fb327-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/ferrilab/bitvec", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260923T224204Z-99cb2060", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/aeef0be672538b8f6694f464bd947084813fb327-1/20260923T224204Z-99cb2060/origin.json": "57af235d64071b6476405362b72badaed1052fba32d8f6a30c290808d95b54a2", "evidence/aeef0be672538b8f6694f464bd947084813fb327-1/20260923T224204Z-99cb2060/proposal.json": "3cd3a2d11efd0dbfab26215e9b177a362c1e5b7a690739ce1caa718eca3610a5"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "bitvec", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Ensure correct buffer size during `Octal::fmt`", "summary": "`Octal::fmt` preallocated a digit buffer of width `usize::BITS / 3` (floor) instead of `ceil(usize::BITS / 3)`, so each storage-element body chunk lost one octal digit. The fix adds `+ (usize::BITS % 3 != 0) as usize`, rounding up.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T22:42:04.086295+00:00"}
